<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The app's own theme colours. Until 2026-10-12 styles.xml named
      @color/colorPrimary, @color/colorPrimaryDark and @color/colorAccent and
      the app defined none, so Capacitor's defaults applied (#3F51B5 indigo,
      #303F9F, and #FF4081 pink for the accent).

      colorPrimary / colorPrimaryDark (2026-10-12, #307): the icon family's
      navy #00286D, the mark's own darkest colour. It is the one icon colour
      that holds white system text and icons (13.78:1; the teal end, #00BB9F,
      gives 2.44:1), and it is the colour the launcher icon starts from, so
      the system's tint for the app and the icon agree.

      colorAccent (2026-10-12, design PR 1): #006784, the same value as the
      web app's --sa-accent in src/styles/tokens.css. It tints the controls
      Android draws itself inside the WebView (selection handles, the text
      cursor, native pickers), so the one accent reaches the parts of the
      screen the stylesheet cannot. Ruled by the owner with the move of the
      screens to the icon family.
    -->
    <color name="colorPrimary">#00286D</color>
    <color name="colorPrimaryDark">#00286D</color>
    <color name="colorAccent">#006784</color>
</resources>
